            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for a water heater, then the Kannada for a resort."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಉಪಹಾರ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಉಪಹಾರ — upahāra — \"breakfast; a light meal\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೋಟೆಲ್ನಲ್ಲಿ ಉಪಹಾರಕ್ಕೆ ಇಡ್ಲಿ ಮತ್ತು ದೋಸೆ ಇತ್ತು. hōṭelnalli upahārakke iḍli mattu dōse ittu. At the hotel there were idlis and dosas for breakfast."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬೆಳಗಿನ ಉಪಹಾರ (upahāra), morning breakfast; ತಿಂಡಿ is the everyday word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಉಪಹಾರ (upahāra) is borrowed from Sanskrit: Monier-Williams gives upahāra as \"an offering, a present\". The sense of a light meal is a later Indian one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
